From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:59:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vdec: bound the DMC idle wait when disabling a decoder port

dec_dmc_port_ctrl(0, ...) clears the decoder's request bit in DMC_REQ_CTRL
and then spins until the channel status register reports the port idle,
with no limit. If the decoder is wedged and its memory port never drains,
the spin never ends. On an S905X5 this is what made a stuck amvdec_h264mvc
fatal: vdec_release() reaches it through vdec_disable_DMC() with
amstream_mutex held, so the closing process could not be killed, every
other amstream user blocked behind the mutex, and reboot never completed.

Give up after 100 ms, log the status register, the mask and DMC_REQ_CTRL,
and carry on, as vdec_stop_armrisc() already does for the AMRISC DMA
waits. The function is also reached from vdec_reset_core(),
hevc_reset_core() and the input context save, where the caller's context
is not known to allow sleeping, so the wait polls with udelay(1) and a
loop count rather than sleeping or relying on jiffies advancing.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
index 29e4410..9704863 100644
--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
@@ -936,8 +936,11 @@ static void hevc_arb_ctrl(bool enable)
 	}
 }
 
+#define DMC_IDLE_TIMEOUT_US 100000
+
 static void dec_dmc_port_ctrl(bool dmc_on, u32 target)
 {
+	int wait_us;
 	unsigned long flags;
 	unsigned int sts_reg_addr = DMC_CHAN_STS;
 	unsigned int mask = 0;
@@ -1028,9 +1031,16 @@ static void dec_dmc_port_ctrl(bool dmc_on, u32 target)
 			sts_reg_addr = DMC_CHAN_STS;
 			break;
 		}
-		while (!(codec_dmcbus_read(sts_reg_addr)
-				& mask))
-				;
+		for (wait_us = 0; wait_us < DMC_IDLE_TIMEOUT_US; wait_us++) {
+			if (codec_dmcbus_read(sts_reg_addr) & mask)
+				break;
+			udelay(1);
+		}
+		if (wait_us == DMC_IDLE_TIMEOUT_US)
+			pr_err("%s: target %u port not idle after %d us, sts reg 0x%x = 0x%x, mask 0x%x, req ctrl 0x%x\n",
+				__func__, target, DMC_IDLE_TIMEOUT_US,
+				sts_reg_addr, codec_dmcbus_read(sts_reg_addr),
+				mask, codec_dmcbus_read(DMC_REQ_CTRL));
 	}
 }
 
